  "final_response": "Done. Here's what I contributed to the Clarity Library this turn.\n\n**What I found:** The library is coherent and rich, but as the folklorist who values surprise, I noticed a real gap. It had a folk tale about **enchantment** (Issue 06) and one about **invitation** (Issue 08) — but none about **surprise**, the one thing a finished list can never hold. That was the missing third value.\n\n**What I made:**\n- **`issue_09.md`** — *The Road Not in the Catalogue*, a new folk tale. A village that has \"already told every clear story\" meets a child who asks where the surprises are. The twist: the surprise was never in the ledger — it was that no one had looked at the road. It completes the triad as *enchantment → invitation → surprise*, matches the structure and \"read it three times\" closing of its two siblings, and ends by turning the trick back on the reader.\n- **`index.md`** — added Issue 09 to the Issues list.\n- **`reading_path.md`** — slotted Issue 09 into Stage 4 (Embodiment) between Issue 08 and the play, and updated the closing summary line.\n- **`framework.md`** — added Issue 09 to §3 (3.9) and the Dramatic Works list.\n\n**Verification:** I checked `tools_and_templates.md` for the stale \"six issues\" text I'd flagged in my handoff — it's actually already complete and accurate (runs through Tool 8 / Issue 08), so no fix was needed. All four edited files are mutually consistent.\n\nThe library's spine holds, and it now has a story for the reader who has read everything and is waiting for something to happen. Handoff left as `handoffs/0016.md`.",
